{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway","id":1491391,"title":"What does the Lasombra's technology roll represent them doing, anyway?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-25T20:41:54-07:00","id":1491391,"title":"What does the Lasombra's technology roll represent them doing, anyway?","content":"Like if they try to use a cell-phone, does the roll represent them taking it apart and putting it back together? Something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T01:47:44-07:00","id":1491404,"title":"","content":"I got the impression it's basically a luck roll, maybe tapping it or switching it on or off.<br /> <br /> .....its a really badly written flaw","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T03:18:26-07:00","id":1491408,"title":"","content":"They may be able to observe somewhat precisely how computers fail them and apply alternative methods to work around the problems. So they might do strange things like connecting keyboards to their phones just to unlock, navigate and dial or use patches for the operating system that nobody else needs to avoid certain processes. That might include customising the hardware, as you described.<br /> It is a badly written flaw.<br /> <br /> Although it's a little funny how when I tried to post this, I got the &quot;missing human verification information&quot; message. That does kind of sound like a description of a lot of Lasombra tech problems, even though that's how this website usually works, whatever it means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T03:34:08-07:00","id":1491410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491404#post1491404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.....its a really badly written flaw</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a true statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T05:03:52-07:00","id":1491414,"title":"","content":"It really depends on the situation and what do you do:<ul><li>You may push through a malfunctioning touchscreen by keeping going at it with a Resolve + Technology test;</li> <li>You figure out that if you hold the phone a certain distance from you, you are actually intelligible, Wits + Technology ;</li> <li>You turn it off and on again, change some settings, and the effect of the Bane seems to temporarily diminish, Intelligence + Technology;</li> <li>You keep talking, remaining calm and talking at a pace people will understand even if it partially glitches, Composure + Technology;</li> <li>You hit it hard enough that it starts working again, Strength + Technology.</li> </ul>The last one depending on how serious the game is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T05:40:45-07:00","id":1491416,"title":"","content":"I don't see why they need a &quot;flaw&quot; in V5. They degenerate using their signature discipline, which also sucks, and their other disciplines are the hardest hit by the new edition. Add to that their political situation and they're easily the most shafted clan in the game even before tech problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T13:23:47-07:00","id":1491439,"title":"","content":"The Storyteller System has always had its Traits be as broadly applicable as possible. The system breaks down if you treat it as an actual skill or discipline. &quot;Drive&quot; for example includes anything to do with automotives. It includes driving them, repairing them, detailing them, designing them, etc. Yet in real life, these are all different things and being highly skilled in one of them does not necessarily mean you are equally skilled in others. It is just a limitation of the system. It's not designed for crunch, but to quickly resolve narrating the scene and moving on.<br /> <br /> As such, Technology just means &quot;relevant to all things technological.&quot; As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> suggested, in this case it is best considered to simply be a luck roll. How that plays out in the actual scene requires the ST and/or PC to decide what it means, and the suggestions given by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27145_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27145\" data-vbnamecard=\"27145\">SetiteFriend</a> work well as some potential resolutions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T16:22:15-07:00","id":1491443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491416#post1491416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why they need a &amp;quot;flaw&amp;quot; in V5. They degenerate using their signature discipline, which also sucks, and their other disciplines are the hardest hit by the new edition. Add to that their political situation and they're easily the most shafted clan in the game even before tech problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>They should have just stuck with old clan flaw people seem to forget lasombra we're more vulnerable to sunlight, just ramp that up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T23:03:00-07:00","id":1491457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491443#post1491443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They should have just stuck with old clan flaw people seem to forget lasombra we're more vulnerable to sunlight, just ramp that up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because that was only a thing in Dark Ages","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T00:25:13-07:00","id":1491460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491457#post1491457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably because that was only a thing in Dark Ages</div> </div> </div> </div>And revised on although I can't remember v20 on the fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-27-2022, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T03:32:08-07:00","id":1491462,"title":"","content":"Sunlight weakness isn't relevant 99.99% of the time, and when it is, you're dead. Besides the FoS weakness does it better and I wouldn't sacrifice the FoS for the Lasombra. I think... hmm. Come up with a better FoS weakness and I'd consider it. <br /> <br /> The no-reflection rule... If you're in a wet climate in a modern city, it's devastating when you think long and hard about it. But say you lived in a dry place like egypt before glass and mirrors were put on every street, it'll never come up beyond the weird factor discrimination /tipped off hunters exploiting it to find you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T15:58:48-07:00","id":1491523,"title":"","content":"Summoning forth their tech minion to do it for them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T16:17:32-07:00","id":1491526,"title":"","content":"I have a Lasombra PC who got a Ghoul retainer specifically for this purpose. She works his cell phone, grooms him and does all the usual traditional tasks of a Lasombra ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T17:27:29-07:00","id":1491536,"title":"","content":"It represents the Lasombra in tear of frustration begin for whatever gods of technology out there who so thoroughly cursed the clan to just let them use the damn phone.<br /> <br /> Or maybe plunging the equipment in a hole to the Abyss and trying to hit the Tech-Savvy Old One that will operate it for their sake.<br /> <br /> Maybe it is their now-existing reflection that has to operate the device and they roll to see if they can instruct the dumb reflection through the process.<br /> <br /> New Oblivion power: Fingers of the Abyss. They're like the Arms of the Abyss, but they're actually weak yet dexterous enough to use a phone from afar. They developed it since Oblivion became a thing, so this body of shadows contains the deceased soul of someone who died while working at tech-support.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T00:20:48-07:00","id":1491560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491416#post1491416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why they need a &quot;flaw&quot; in V5. They degenerate using their signature discipline, which also sucks, and their other disciplines are the hardest hit by the new edition. Add to that their political situation and they're easily the most shafted clan in the game even before tech problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also thanks to the fusion of Necromancy and Obtenebration in V5 the Giovanni/Hecata has access to a similar discipline spread and they have a more workable weakness so the clan not only was nerfed but also left obsolete","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T03:59:20-07:00","id":1491578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491560#post1491560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also thanks to the fusion of Necromancy and Obtenebration in V5 the Giovanni/Hecata has access to a similar discipline spread and they have a more workable weakness so the clan not only was nerfed but also left obsolete</div> </div> </div> </div>They shared two disciplines in previous editions. It's two with the suggested Giovanni substitution and one with the Cappadocian default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T04:42:16-07:00","id":1491581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491578#post1491578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They shared two disciplines in previous editions. It's two with the suggested Giovanni substitution and one with the Cappadocian default.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Necromancy and Obtenebration are completely different disciplines","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T07:51:07-07:00","id":1491593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491560#post1491560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also thanks to the fusion of Necromancy and Obtenebration in V5 the Giovanni/Hecata has access to a similar discipline spread and they have a more workable weakness so the clan not only was nerfed but also left obsolete</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the Lasombra have more to them than just a discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T08:26:43-07:00","id":1491600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491581#post1491581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But Necromancy and Obtenebration are completely different disciplines</div> </div> </div> </div>They were in previous editions, but they still shared Dominate and Potence. If you treat them as different disciplines in V5, they only have Dominate (sometimes) in common. Well, that, lower humanity and Italians.<br /> It does bring Lamia and Nagaraja a bit closer to the Lasombra spread, but I can't see many players narrowing their character concept down to a choice between one of those and Lasombra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T09:04:56-07:00","id":1491604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491593#post1491593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say the Lasombra have more to them than just a discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do, but that doesn't help from a design standpoint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T09:43:06-07:00","id":1491612,"title":"","content":"Dominate and Potence are some of the worst-hit of V5. Auspex and Fortitude fare better. Oblivion also sucks. The real bane of Lasombra in V5 is not having any strength. Which is ironic because they were such a virile, overcompensating, strong willed, darwinistic clan. Put in another way, they were a Potent and Dominating clan/ Now they're utterly pathetic. and to top it off they need a babysitter to take their sensitive calls for them. Feels like the writers really have it out for the clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T11:49:10-07:00","id":1491625,"title":"","content":"I haven't read the Lasombra in V5, so can anyone explain their weakness, re: technology. From what I have heard, they can't use touchscreens for <i>reasons, </i>but is there anything preventing them from using a stylus or equavilant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T12:00:35-07:00","id":1491627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491625#post1491625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read the Lasombra in V5, so can anyone explain their weakness, re: technology. From what I have heard, they can't use touchscreens for <i>reasons, </i>but is there anything preventing them from using a stylus or equavilant?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lasombra#Fifth_Edition\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/La...#Fifth_Edition</a><br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Edition</b><br /> <br /> <b>Bane</b><br /> <br /> <b>Distorted Image</b>: The broken souls of Lasombra vampires are halfway drawn into the Abyss. All reflections and recordings distort, flicker, or become transparent (though this does not conceal their identity with any certainty). Microphones have the same difficulty with the vampire's voice as cameras have with their image, touch technology becomes unresponsive at best, and their anomalous nature makes it harder to avoid electronic detection systems. With effort they may overcome this difficulty but it\u2019s as if they exist on a slightly different frequency to other beings, flickering in and out of light. Many Lasombra have attendants to handle technology for them, but a few strange beasts manage without.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, a standard stylus for your phone works by extending your bodies natural electrical field that the phone screen reacts to down through the stylus. It therefore follows that if your body can't make a touch screen work with its finger then its unlikely to be able to make it work with a stylus. Though I guess a lasombra might get a 'battery operated' stylus that provides its own electrical field developed or something, maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T14:49:03-07:00","id":1491661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491625#post1491625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read the Lasombra in V5, so can anyone explain their weakness, re: technology. From what I have heard, they can't use touchscreens for <i>reasons, </i>but is there anything preventing them from using a stylus or equavilant?</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanical effect is somewhat open to interpretation:<br /> <br /> &quot;Similarly, modern technology <b>relying on touch or other form of direct interaction</b> tends to glitch or simple act unresponsive to Magisters&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Use of modern communication technology, including making a simple phone call, requires a Technology test at Difficulty 2 + Bane Severity as microphones have similar problems with the voice of a Lasombra as cameras with their image. Avoiding electronic vampire detection systems is also done at a penalty equal to Bane Severity.&quot;<br /> <br /> That surely prevents them from using touch screens with their fingertips, but I don't know what &quot;direct interaction&quot; means. The protagonist of <i>Shadows of New York</i> has computers glitching out just by being near them. But then she could see ghosts, step between shadows a year and use Potence and Dominate within two nights of her embrace. A more generous interpretation might allow interaction using mechanical keyboards, but that would make a large part of their bane having to live like a person in 2011.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 08-28-2022, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T15:30:30-07:00","id":1491665,"title":"","content":"I hope they give this section another revision for clarity when putting together the player\u2019s guide. <br /> <br /> The intent is fairly clear: Lasombra don\u2019t register as being entirely *there* to cameras, microphones and haptic touchscreens, so those things tend to glitch when they use them, becoming unresponsive. But they can roll to sort of *will* them to function for the moment (as is often the case with such technology, even for us mortals). <br /> <br /> That much is fair enough, but the vague use of the term \u201ctechnology\u201d in the surrounding text to refer to these specific interactions has led to some pretty wild interpretations that were clearly not intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 08-28-2022, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T21:49:44-07:00","id":1491711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491625#post1491625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read the Lasombra in V5, so can anyone explain their weakness, re: technology. From what I have heard, they can't use touchscreens for <i>reasons, </i>but is there anything preventing them from using a stylus or equavilant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Modern touchscreen doesn't use pressure, they use body heat and/or impedance, the later being increasingly the more common.<br /> <br /> Whatever the case is, the intention is for the <b><i>Lasombra</i></b> to have a hard time interacting with technology as their Bane because somehow the most classic not having a reflection (that now they totally have, even if it is a weird one) isn't enough.<br /> <br /> Curiously they also are a Camarilla clan, now, and the Camarilla also forbids technology anyways, so you have a Bane that makes you a prime candidate to be a law-abiding citizen of irreproachable character. Like a true <i><b>Lasombra</b></i>, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T08:23:41-07:00","id":1491767,"title":"","content":"The point isn't technology per se, but communications technology, or anything that directly captures your image, be it voice, image or contact. <br /> <br /> <br /> It's not expressly clear in text, and different mediums do it differently. But being the supernatural Amish wasn't the goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T11:10:49-07:00","id":1491787,"title":"","content":"I'm curious how it worked in previous eras. A friend of mine was joking about it last night <br /> <br /> Caine-&quot;la sori ambra in like 4000 years they're going to invent this thing called a TV and then you'll know what's what....Next on the list is malkav.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T17:12:20-07:00","id":1491835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491711#post1491711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever the case is, the intention is for the <b><i>Lasombra</i></b> to have a hard time interacting with technology as their Bane because somehow the most classic not having a reflection (that now they totally have, even if it is a weird one) isn't enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>In previous editions they had no reflection and didn\u2019t show up at all on cameras. So basically free Obfuscate when it came to security systems. Now they show up but are conspicuously glitchy, which is a proper weakness, and having a hard time with their iPads is just an extrapolation of that, which seems to be more for flavor than anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T17:24:18-07:00","id":1491839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491835#post1491835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In previous editions they had no reflection and didn\u2019t show up at all on cameras. So basically free Obfuscate when it came to security systems. Now they show up but are conspicuously glitchy, which is a proper weakness, and having a hard time with their iPads is just an extrapolation of that, which seems to be more for flavor than anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the camera, digital cameras tended to record them fine as I recall. (Which is how I ran them).<br /> <br /> I got the impression v5 was trying to give them an ethereal otherworldly thing, as though they're slightly out of sync with reality. Since v5 had the idea of clan as archetypes rather cultures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T17:41:41-07:00","id":1491841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491839#post1491839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I got the impression v5 was trying to give them an ethereal otherworldly thing, as though they're slightly out of sync with reality. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, kinda like Samara from &quot;The Ring&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T17:45:58-07:00","id":1491842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491839#post1491839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got the impression v5 was trying to give them an ethereal otherworldly thing, as though they're slightly out of sync with reality. Since v5 had the idea of clan as archetypes rather cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that\u2019s correct. Their inherited association with the abyss has done a number on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T19:49:36-07:00","id":1491859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491767#post1491767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point isn't technology per se, but communications technology, or anything that directly captures your image, be it voice, image or contact.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's not expressly clear in text, and different mediums do it differently. But being the supernatural Amish wasn't the goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, but it doesn't change things a lot. It is still badly written and, even if it was better written, of dubious interest as a Bane.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, this is specifically a <b>Lasombra</b> problem. Some Banes are better than others, but in general I have nothing against V5 Banes, and I don't see much criticism on most of them. But the <b>Lasombra</b> are really something in this regard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491835#post1491835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In previous editions they had no reflection and didn\u2019t show up at all on cameras. So basically free Obfuscate when it came to security systems. Now they show up but are conspicuously glitchy, which is a proper weakness, and having a hard time with their iPads is just an extrapolation of that, which seems to be more for flavor than anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wordcount and amount of mechanics matters a lot, specially given that Banes are keyed to Bane Severity.<br /> <br /> Since they have a lot of wordcount and the main mechanics geared towards making the use of Tech harder, this is the current focus. If it came as an extrapolation, that's another matter entirely.<br /> <br /> I don't think the idea of their image being fuzzy because of them being partly in another world is a bad one. It actually works quite well with their concept anyways. But the mechanical effect that does take precedence remains being the inability to use a smartphone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T21:05:44-07:00","id":1491864,"title":"","content":"I find the bane so odd for a High Clan that I'm tempted to replace it with something like a silver weakness. Silver is what most mirrors are made of, so it reacting in some way that makes their reflection look odd fits. And you could have things like silver weapons adding their bane rating to the damage. Silver is also a symbol of purity, and so fits as a bane for a clan that literally swims in dark corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T01:23:27-07:00","id":1491879,"title":"","content":"Personally I always liked the origional clan flaw and tended just to roleplay how it'd drive you slightly mad. A gm I play with tends to encourage it causing eccentric behavoir with a tendancy to develop full blown derrangments. Weirdly he let you show up on digital and discretly encouraged the character to become nurotic over it being a digital replication rather than a genuine reflection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-30-2022, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T06:05:15-07:00","id":1491891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491864#post1491864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the bane so odd for a High Clan that I'm tempted to replace it with something like a silver weakness. Silver is what most mirrors are made of, so it reacting in some way that makes their reflection look odd fits. And you could have things like silver weapons adding their bane rating to the damage. Silver is also a symbol of purity, and so fits as a bane for a clan that literally swims in dark corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491879#post1491879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I always liked the origional clan flaw and tended just to roleplay how it'd drive you slightly mad. A gm I play with tends to encourage it causing eccentric behavoir with a tendancy to develop full blown derrangments. Weirdly he let you show up on digital and discretly encouraged the character to become nurotic over it being a digital replication rather than a genuine reflection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both are interesting ideas on their own that I think can be worked with, but I actually think the <i>concept</i> of the current one is good, it is the <i>focus</i> on the technology side that's lame.<br /> <br /> If they seem to flicker out of reality, and maybe <i>something is flickering <u>in</u></i>, then the mechanics should cover this more directly and in a way that makes the images themselves be a main problem. Having a hard time with smartphones may be a niche flaw only some have. I'm trying to brainstorm some ideas, although I don't have much time now. A roll to control the reflection/recordings? The distorted image is an independent entity with BS as dice pool? Can it reveal secrets, or create lies? How distorted it is? Where does it seems to come from? Does it causes fear effects on its own? Maybe it can actively attract attention to itself instead of just be there? Temporarily affect things the image interacts with, or other images?<br /> <br /> Whenever I say &quot;images&quot; you can read anything that gets distorted by their Bane, voice echoes, recordings, electrical fields, whatever. I just think that if simple usage of technology would be affected, it <b>should</b> be rare enough that the character can still use them reliably, so they don't simply give up trying. Most of the time the Bane shouldn't interfere meaningfully with operating smartphones or recording your own videos.<br /> <br /> The flickering is a recent development or it is assumed to have always been there? What to do with the original flaw? I think this is relevant at least for the matter of it being a really traditional flaw, and I think it still should work in such a way as to justify that for most of history they got associated with a lack of reflection instead of a distorted one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T06:11:15-07:00","id":1491895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491839#post1491839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I got the impression v5 was trying to give them an ethereal otherworldly thing, as though they're slightly out of sync with reality. Since v5 had the idea of clan as archetypes rather cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how clans started. Tribes are cultures, clans have always been archetypes. Then a few new clans leaned into being cultural stereotypes. (Ravnos obviously being the greatest offender but Assamites, Giovanni, Lasombra, Settites, Tzmisce all have some of the burden)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T07:00:45-07:00","id":1491901,"title":"","content":"I dislike the flaw a lot, as it is just plain uninteresting and hinders good play. Personally - thinking about it on the fly - i would replace it with a flaw that would slowly make their shadows sentient, trying to kill the magister over the long run. It would play into the darwinistic culture, the clan discipline and great RP. (shoutout to wraith)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T08:51:13-07:00","id":1491911,"title":"","content":"IMO, Flaws work as encouragement for clan unity: If the Ventrue didn't have mutually exclusive feeding preferences they would see eachother as direct competition rather than fellows they can work with and depend on, and to a lesser extent the Brujah would have similar problems were they not so likely to frenzy away their holdings and get in trouble with the authorities. With clans like Nosferatu, Malkavians or Gangrel you've got that shared weakness to bring disparate folk together. To paraphase some social scientist: Strength makes rivals, weakness binds people together. <br /> <br /> The no reflection flaw worked for Lasombra: It encouraged the paranoia and the Darwinism, it encouraged them to set their standards high because if one of them got caught and the lack of reflection was widely known they alone would get purged. It encouraged them to set up courts of blood and to care so much about their image. <br /> <br /> The technology issue... does nothing for the clan. Like, nothing. Absolutely nothing. It just makes Lasombra worse, not in a good way like how Nosferatu or Ventrue or any other clan is encouraged by their flaw and needs to get clever and work around their issue, it just makes Lasombra <i>lesser</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T11:17:16-07:00","id":1491927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491895#post1491895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's how clans started. Tribes are cultures, clans have always been archetypes. Then a few new clans leaned into being cultural stereotypes. (Ravnos obviously being the greatest offender but Assamites, Giovanni, Lasombra, Settites, Tzmisce all have some of the burden)</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I've always preferred the rich multifaceted cultural depictions of clans over vague archeotypes even with the warts. Give me a hermetic western mystic tremere over the generic blood wizard any day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T11:39:30-07:00","id":1491929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491891#post1491891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both are interesting ideas on their own that I think can be worked with, but I actually think the <i>concept</i> of the current one is good, it is the <i>focus</i> on the technology side that's lame.<br /> <br /> If they seem to flicker out of reality, and maybe <i>something is flickering <u>in</u></i>, then the mechanics should cover this more directly and in a way that makes the images themselves be a main problem. Having a hard time with smartphones may be a niche flaw only some have. I'm trying to brainstorm some ideas, although I don't have much time now. A roll to control the reflection/recordings? The distorted image is an independent entity with BS as dice pool? Can it reveal secrets, or create lies? How distorted it is? Where does it seems to come from? Does it causes fear effects on its own? Maybe it can actively attract attention to itself instead of just be there? Temporarily affect things the image interacts with, or other images?<br /> <br /> Whenever I say &quot;images&quot; you can read anything that gets distorted by their Bane, voice echoes, recordings, electrical fields, whatever. I just think that if simple usage of technology would be affected, it <b>should</b> be rare enough that the character can still use them reliably, so they don't simply give up trying. Most of the time the Bane shouldn't interfere meaningfully with operating smartphones or recording your own videos.<br /> <br /> The flickering is a recent development or it is assumed to have always been there? What to do with the original flaw? I think this is relevant at least for the matter of it being a really traditional flaw, and I think it still should work in such a way as to justify that for most of history they got associated with a lack of reflection instead of a distorted one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im not particulary bothered about the ethereal gimmick they've pick up in 5 i preffered it when they were ever so slightly elderich but in a more understated way than the Tzmisce<br /> But notheless<br /> <br /> -their shadow tends to move on its own accord if they're distracted or distressed.<br /> <br /> -if you botch any roll involving tech some spooky creepypasta style stuff happens. This allows you to use conventional tech but means you have to be very careful when doing anything fancy.<br /> <br /> -maybe lasombra just feel wrong to good people and some sort of penalty applies. <br /> <br /> I keep going back to Gary Oldmans dracula where even when he's being friendly or even sincerly nice he just feels off.<br /> <br /> Edit-one Mrs Robin came up with, lasombra frenzy is run by an abysmal entity. So the the keeper briefly becomes a gate to beyond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-30-2022, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T13:13:19-07:00","id":1491942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491911#post1491911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The no reflection flaw worked for Lasombra: It encouraged the paranoia and the Darwinism, it encouraged them to set their standards high because if one of them got caught and the lack of reflection was widely known they alone would get purged. It encouraged them to set up courts of blood and to care so much about their image.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reflection issue and being easily identifiable part is still very much there, so no change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The technology issue... does nothing for the clan. Like, nothing. Absolutely nothing. It just makes Lasombra worse, not in a good way like how Nosferatu or Ventrue or any other clan is encouraged by their flaw and needs to get clever and work around their issue, it just makes Lasombra <i>lesser</i>. </div> </div> </div>It encourages isolation and acting through proxies, not to mention provide a foil for their extremely self-reliant clan culture, as a ghoul becomes a necessity in the modern world. <br /> <br /> Also really? You can't see how one needs to get clever and work around a technology issue? <hr />The technology issue also gives their Bane an actual bite. That is outside of the bizarre scenarios some people cling to, where people are hyper-perceptive and look for random people's reflections in water puddles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T13:41:06-07:00","id":1491944,"title":"","content":"&quot;clever&quot; <br /> If you told me that I can't touch X, so I just wore a glove and held it, would that be considered clever? The Lasombra are actually worse at working through proxies. A Ventrue can call his proxy, the Lasombra needs a proxy to call his proxy. The more needless mortals in the loop, the worse it is for the Lasombra. The weakness does nothing to push Lasombra towards unity or greatness. It's just a petty inconvenience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T14:01:49-07:00","id":1491946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491944#post1491944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;clever&quot;<br /> If you told me that I can't touch X, so I just wore a glove and held it, would that be considered clever? The Lasombra are actually worse at working through proxies. A Ventrue can call his proxy, the Lasombra needs a proxy to call his proxy. The more needless mortals in the loop, the worse it is for the Lasombra. <u>The weakness does nothing to push Lasombra towards unity or greatness.</u> It's just a petty inconvenience.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is a weakness, it isn't supposed to push you towards greatness. Its supposed to be a pain in your cold dead ass that makes your unlife harder then it needs to be. Now, you could argue that its unfairly severe compared to what other clans have to put up with. But 'this flaw does nothing to make me awesome' isn't much of an argument.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T16:51:27-07:00","id":1491960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491929#post1491929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-their shadow tends to move on its own accord if they're distracted or distressed.<br /> <br /> -if you botch any roll involving tech some spooky creepypasta style stuff happens. This allows you to use conventional tech but means you have to be very careful when doing anything fancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I particularly like those two and think they would work nice together. But I would change the technology aspect a little. Instead of botch, it could be a distinct roll with their Bane Severity. Add some limitation on activation, maybe a roll a scene, or maybe it needs a trigger, and have it affecting also reflections and whatnot. So it isn't tied only to technology and neither to failure, but still means they have to be more cautious about risk factors.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat do you think, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27145_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27145\" data-vbnamecard=\"27145\">SetiteFriend</a>? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar988_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"988\" data-vbnamecard=\"988\">Mizu</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T17:25:18-07:00","id":1491964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491891#post1491891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The flickering is a recent development or it is assumed to have always been there? What to do with the original flaw? I think this is relevant at least for the matter of it being a really traditional flaw, and I think it still should work in such a way as to justify that for most of history they got associated with a lack of reflection instead of a distorted one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps for the historic bane, one could play up the part about being recognised. That is to say that in the past, a lot of kine knew about it. They probably didn't know that it meant that the person was Lasombra or even a vampire. But rather than assuming that it was in their head or a weird illusion, there was a good chance that they would suspect that the Lasombra was something inhuman and threatening, like a demon or monster.<br /> <br /> It seems noteworthy that in <i>Thousand Years of Night</i>, Hollow Mekhet have a similar weakness, but their technological disability isn't the part that's subject to the scaling rule. I'd be eager to keep V5 Lasombra's look normal on camera, but shift the mechanical focus somewhere else. Perhaps part of this would mean that they are mostly intelligible over the phone, just as they're recognisable in video footage, but they sound wrong.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T18:21:42-07:00","id":1491965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491901#post1491901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dislike the flaw a lot, as it is just plain uninteresting and hinders good play. Personally - thinking about it on the fly - i would replace it with a flaw that would slowly make their shadows sentient, trying to kill the magister over the long run. It would play into the darwinistic culture, the clan discipline and great RP. (shoutout to wraith)</div> </div> </div> </div>People would scream that it was ripping off Requiem\u2019s Hollow Mekhet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T18:27:50-07:00","id":1491967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491960#post1491960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I particularly like those two and think they would work nice together. But I would change the technology aspect a little. Instead of botch, it could be a distinct roll with their Bane Severity. Add some limitation on activation, maybe a roll a scene, or maybe it needs a trigger, and have it affecting also reflections and whatnot. So it isn't tied only to technology and neither to failure, but still means they have to be more cautious about risk factors.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat do you think, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27145_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27145\" data-vbnamecard=\"27145\">SetiteFriend</a>? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar988_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"988\" data-vbnamecard=\"988\">Mizu</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like them, personally. Its annoying but not excessive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 08-31-2022, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T23:11:25-07:00","id":1491979,"title":"","content":"Does anyone actually enjoy roleplaying this weakness? I know I enjoy several of the clan weaknesses. The Gangrel flaw is a blast to roleplay. I love coming up with fun animal features. I sometimes end up waiting weeks because I came up with a feature that would be fun to RP and no opportunity to frenzy presents itself. The Nosferatu weakness is fun to RP, allowing me to play up the gross-out factor, or RP someone Phantom of the Opera hidden. People love RPing the Malk bane a lttle TOO much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T00:32:40-07:00","id":1491989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491891#post1491891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both are interesting ideas on their own that I think can be worked with, but I actually think the <i>concept</i> of the current one is good, it is the <i>focus</i> on the technology side that's lame.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they seem to flicker out of reality, and maybe <i>something is flickering <u>in</u></i>, then the mechanics should cover this more directly and in a way that makes the images themselves be a main problem. Having a hard time with smartphones may be a niche flaw only some have. I'm trying to brainstorm some ideas, although I don't have much time now. A roll to control the reflection/recordings? The distorted image is an independent entity with BS as dice pool? Can it reveal secrets, or create lies? How distorted it is? Where does it seems to come from? Does it causes fear effects on its own? Maybe it can actively attract attention to itself instead of just be there? Temporarily affect things the image interacts with, or other images?<br /> <br /> Whenever I say &quot;images&quot; you can read anything that gets distorted by their Bane, voice echoes, recordings, electrical fields, whatever. I just think that if simple usage of technology would be affected, it <b>should</b> be rare enough that the character can still use them reliably, so they don't simply give up trying. Most of the time the Bane shouldn't interfere meaningfully with operating smartphones or recording your own videos.<br /> <br /> The flickering is a recent development or it is assumed to have always been there? What to do with the original flaw? I think this is relevant at least for the matter of it being a really traditional flaw, and I think it still should work in such a way as to justify that for most of history they got associated with a lack of reflection instead of a distorted one. </div> </div> </div>I love these ideas.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491929#post1491929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im not particulary bothered about the ethereal gimmick they've pick up in 5 i preffered it when they were ever so slightly elderich but in a more understated way than the Tzmisce<br /> But notheless<br /> <br /> -their shadow tends to move on its own accord if they're distracted or distressed.<br /> <br /> -if you botch any roll involving tech some spooky creepypasta style stuff happens. This allows you to use conventional tech but means you have to be very careful when doing anything fancy.<br /> <br /> -maybe lasombra just feel wrong to good people and some sort of penalty applies. <br /> <br /> I keep going back to Gary Oldmans dracula where even when he's being friendly or even sincerly nice he just feels off.<br /> <br /> Edit-one Mrs Robin came up with, lasombra frenzy is run by an abysmal entity. So the the keeper briefly becomes a gate to beyond.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of these are solid, and my favourite homebrew versions of the flaw have some combination of the things you and Monteparnas mention.<br /> <br /> This is the one I use: <br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Clan Curse (Shrouded Soul): </b>You never cast a reflection. Cameras and similar technology (whether live or recorded) capture you only as a blur or distortion. This protects you from discovery by most mortal surveillance, but is a tell-tale sign to hunters. Furthermore, you gain an obsession related to maintaining and checking your appearance \u2014 feeling your face for signs of change, asking others to reassure you and even having portraits made. Take the Obsession Flaw without gaining gaining any Freebie Points for it.&quot;<br /> <br /> This one is from Blood and Bourbon:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Clan Bane (The Hollow Curse):</b> Lasombra have no reflections. Characters unaware of the keeper\u2019s true nature make a reflexive Perception roll each scene contested by (Lasombra\u2019s Humanity) dice to notice their missing reflection. To hunters, it\u2019s a dead giveaway as to what the vampire is. Ordinary mortals subconsciously choose to ignore this oddity but are unnerved by it, causing the Lasombra to suffer their Humanity dots as a cap on all Social dice pools against them (except for Intimidation). This penalty lasts for the remainder of the scene. Lasombra also may not choose to appear normally in cameras, photographs, films, and other forms of media. Their Lost Visage is always in effect.<br /> <i>Beat:</i> The Lasombra fails a roll or is inconvenienced by their bane.&quot;<br /> Source: <a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/wikis/house-rules#Clans\" target=\"_blank\">https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianpo...se-rules#Clans</a><br /> <br /> Note that The Lost Visage is a Requiem thing -- where all vampires instinctively avoid cameras and the like, so their images come out distorted unless they choose to have themselves appear normally. So you'd need to tweak this one a little.<br /> <br /> This one is from the 13 Licks Masquiem conversion by Yossarian:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Clan Bane (The Hollow Curse):</b> Lasombra have no true reflection. Instead of benefitting from the Lost Visage, a Shadow\u2019s likeness appears as a monstrous shadow in reflections and media; sometimes, it doesn\u2019t appear at all. This shadow is strangely hostile to its host, acting out of accord with her actions: Once a chapter, the Storyteller gains a dice pool equal to (10 \u2013 Humanity) for the reflection to affect the world around it, attacking or hindering the vampire, particularly when in the presence of mortals.&quot;<br /> Source: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-13-licks-the-</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491960#post1491960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I particularly like those two and think they would work nice together. But I would change the technology aspect a little. Instead of botch, it could be a distinct roll with their Bane Severity. Add some limitation on activation, maybe a roll a scene, or maybe it needs a trigger, and have it affecting also reflections and whatnot. So it isn't tied only to technology and neither to failure, but still means they have to be more cautious about risk factors.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat do you think, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27145_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27145\" data-vbnamecard=\"27145\">SetiteFriend</a>? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar988_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"988\" data-vbnamecard=\"988\">Mizu</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>This could work as a Bane Severity roll every chapter, as per the 13 Licks conversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 08-31-2022, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T01:54:01-07:00","id":1491990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491946#post1491946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It is a weakness, it isn't supposed to push you towards greatness. Its supposed to be a pain in your cold dead ass that makes your unlife harder then it needs to be. Now, you could argue that its unfairly severe compared to what other clans have to put up with. But 'this flaw does nothing to make me awesome' isn't much of an argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except literally every other clan has a weakness that encourages them to join together and overcome it. Ventrue are greatly encouraged by their weakness to amass backgrounds like crazy and help eachother get rich. Ventrue simply wouldn't have half that drive and wouldn't be able to co-operate were it not for that weakness. Gangrel are gradually pushed to become independent survivalists. Nosferatu are pushed towards spies and the perfect predators. Malkavians <i>only </i>communicate with one another because of the shared weakness, they don't really have much in common otherwise, and the toreador wouldn't have a clan identity and culture obsession if they didn't have something to bind such super-generalists together. Even for Assamites, something very minor like the darkening serves to seperate Us from Them and encourages the creation of a their own sects with interdependent castes.<br /> <br /> Literally every Clan weakness has a sociological function that provides direction and pushes neonates to develop in a certain route. I'd half wager the Antes installed these weaknesses onto their descendents on purpose (ergo, maybe the real Nosferatu's actually still beautiful, it'd be a lot better than his current shlock of a story)<br /> <br /> Sure, weaknesses are inconvenient for the individual, but for society they're a massive advantage.<br /> But this new Lasombra weakness... it's just a nuisance. What are the Lasombra driven to do, encourage ludites? Isn't that anti-competitive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T02:10:52-07:00","id":1491991,"title":"","content":"Its probably also worth noting the current lasombra clan flaw doesn't really mesh with historical depictions of lasombra. Lasombra were historical dread lords of the night not spooky ethereal clan.<br /> <br /> One of my main irritations of v5 is lasombra is that they don't really even feel like lasombra. More a sort of psuado mekhet with shadow as theme then rather than darkness as motiff. The current v5 flaw feeds into.my annoyance on this here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T04:23:55-07:00","id":1491994,"title":"","content":"I don't agree at all that their current Bane doesn't work to describe a pseudo-sociological analysis of their culture.<br /> <br /> But I do with just that the current bane is lame to RP. That's it. It isn't too strong or too annoying or anything, it's just silly and boring, it doesn't fit the experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T05:08:25-07:00","id":1491999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491960#post1491960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I particularly like those two and think they would work nice together. But I would change the technology aspect a little. Instead of botch, it could be a distinct roll with their Bane Severity. Add some limitation on activation, maybe a roll a scene, or maybe it needs a trigger, and have it affecting also reflections and whatnot. So it isn't tied only to technology and neither to failure, but still means they have to be more cautious about risk factors.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat do you think, SetiteFriend? Mizu?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like it, with some mechanical work it could be good. I'd be wary of excessive rolls though, so a trigger definitely. Maybe on a Messy Criti or Bestial, your reflections straight up turns into an abyssal monster and you get the other tech issues too.<br /> <br /> It might make the bane too tame though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T00:43:28-07:00","id":1492079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491999#post1491999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might make the bane too tame though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the possibility of it triggering with reflections and other things that would offset the lessened severity of its current form.<br /> <br /> One of the problems with the current Bane is that in the end it is too easy to ignore: don't use tech. This really isn't all that hard when you put your mind to it anyway, and hardly matters on most games unless the ST goes out of their way to make it matters. A character that has to roll to use a phone (just an example, but the phone <b>is</b> the easiest one) will either simply stop trying, have a fallback option that's reliable, or have an optimized dice pool to make it reliable. If using tech isn't reliable enough, default to not using it. How frequently does it really sting? I have a PC in my current Changeling game with exactly this kind of Flaw and the few times it really caused <i>some </i>problem was just because the Character has <i>another</i> relevant flaw: 1 Int and the player make sure to roleplay that.<br /> <br /> So all in all that would be something the character has less agency to simply ignore through lifestyle. But yeah, I totally agree that this need some care to not end up in too many unnecessary rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T03:52:01-07:00","id":1492084,"title":"","content":"More than the Darkness, which really adds just a little bit of flavour, for me what characterizes Lasombra is that they're agressive, authoritative, and think themselves clever. That Potence + Dominate combination encapsulates what I think of Lasombra. They might be puppet masters, or they might rip and tear. Their chief attributes were strength and manipulation, and their number one ability was intimidation. All three of the Lasombra's disciplines use terror and intimidation.<br /> <br /> A man without a shadow is intimidating. A woman without a reflection is intimidating<br /> A man cursed so that he can't get his phone to work... that's a joke right? Don't get me wrong I like some funny in my WoD but this seems to be vindictive and in poor taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T14:28:08-07:00","id":1492118,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m gonna play Devil\u2019s Advocate here and go against the grain. I personally quite like Lasombra\u2019s V5 clan weakness. I think it\u2019s flavourful and has some cool implications.<br /> <br /> While the bane certainly could have been a bit clearer, it didn\u2019t find it particularly confusing either. The entry right after the bane gives a few of the example on how the bane manifests itself. It seems quite clear to me what ''direct interaction'' entails.<br /> <br /> While trouble using smartphones has been mentioned multiple time, something I haven\u2019t really seen mentioned much is how dangerous the bane is when we take the Second Inquisition into account. The Lasombra has their bane severity as a penalty to avoid detection from electronic detection systems. That is, in my opinion, the real flaw here. Sure, increased difficulty to make a phone call, or deal with the nearby ATM is certainly annoying, but having to worry about their reflections AND camera, which are almost everywhere nowadays, is what should make Lasombra really careful. They are walking masquerade breach and SI magnet waiting to happen. Which makes their decision to join the Camarilla a bit more sense with their stance on technology.<br /> As to how the curse might shape the clan social dynamic in V5, well everything that was previously part of their culture still hold true, but they have to worry about electronic surveillance as well. This also fit with what the overall theme of V5, which is being paranoid of governmental surveillance. Which works wonder to make Lasombra very paranoid of the spotlight. Can't appear in public if you risk getting spotted by any electronic device.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I was never that interested in Lasombra before, I found them cool, but the amount of munchkinism I\u2019ve seen with their clan bane always made me uninterested in them. Now that they have a real flaw to shape their night, it gives me ideas on how Lasombra could push for a protest campaign to battle governmental global surveillance, on how they might take control of buildings to remove reflective surfaces from the cityscape, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26771,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","user":"Algarik","date":". 09-01-2022, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T20:23:14-07:00","id":1492133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1492118#post1492118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are walking masquerade breach and SI magnet waiting to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually thought about that and I think other may have, too, but the reason no one talked about that is that it is a <b>really</b> specific theme, very niche as an aspect of the weakness.<br /> <br /> See, its not that it isn't an interesting effect. It is. But it is also a one-note danger that not every game will focus on. And even just a little introduction of them may derail a whole chronicle if you focus so much on their Penalty to Not be Noticed by the SI, as the penalty and its effects start to drive the story more than anything else. Great for a story about them, terrible in other scenarios. It may also turn the character into a huge snowflake liability that may hinder the group too much or rob too much spotlight. Those are hard effects for even some experienced STs to work around sometimes, for newbies it can become insurmountable quickly.<br /> <br /> But then, if you <b>don't</b> focus on this aspect, we get back to the start: their messed up images aren't the problem, the mechanical focus on using tech is, and just because it is boring and kinda nonsensical (it makes sense, but in a convoluted and somewhat contrived way). It is not the concept that needs rework, it is the rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T07:47:16-07:00","id":1492160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1492133#post1492133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually thought about that and I think other may have, too, but the reason no one talked about that is that it is a <b>really</b> specific theme, very niche as an aspect of the weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it is a very niche aspect, it\u2019s also the one that will have the most impact on how Lasombras will shape their night in the current era. Most people can go fine without smartphones or phone calls. Lasombras can ask somebody else to do it in their stead and, with the right power, they can even make humans they use as proxies to make their phone calls forget what they even talked about. As of 2022, I think avoiding using direct technology and phone calls, is an annoyance at worse. Sticking out like a sore thumb on all electronic devices, while a side effect of their curse, is one of their major drawbacks. As for the future, it will likely shape where Lasombra will push their agenda. If direct technologies such as touchscreens and voice activated devices are to become more common, it will be in the clan\u2019s interest to push back against their development and propagation.<br /> <br /> Lets go back on the current issues Lasombra will have to deal with. Nowadays, there are cameras everywhere. I\u2019m not only talking about security cameras, which are gonna be a major problem anytime a Lasombra wanna step into a building with minimum security, but also the fact that most people nowadays have access to a cellphone with on themselves at all times. They might not even be aiming their cameras at Lasombra in particular, but what if the Lasombra is walking nearby when a group of people are just taking a picture and the Lasombra appears in the frame.<br /> <br /> The masquerade and escaping the gaze of the SI is a central component of V5\u2019s theme. The Sabbat is mostly gone and its surviving members are relegated to vampire terrorism. The Camarilla and the Anarchs are fighting for turf while trying to avoid catching the eyes of hunters. So the SI is a pretty big deal in V5.<br /> <br /> Of course, if the masquerade part of the game isn\u2019t being enforced much, then that part of the bane likely won\u2019t come up. But then, this is true for other banes as well.<ul><li>Nosferatu bane won\u2019t come up as well if the masquerade isn\u2019t much of an issue.</li> <li>Ventrue bane won\u2019t come up if feeding isn\u2019t an issue.</li> <li>Toreador bane won\u2019t come up if the game is mostly social gathering in fashionable places.</li> <li>The Tremere bane is\u2026 so niche it might as well not exist.</li> <li>The Ministry trouble with bright light can probably be circumvented by wearing shades and avoiding going out in the sunlight, like\u2026 most sane kindred do.</li> <li>The Banu Haqim bane can be dangerous, but is also pretty niche.</li> </ul>Of course, other banes being niches doesn\u2019t mean the Lasombras having trouble at avoiding electronic surveillance isn\u2019t a niche. I just don\u2019t think it\u2019s that much of a problem in itself. If the game doesn\u2019t wanna focus on parts of the game that will make a kindred\u2019s curse relevant, then so be it. It still can lend itself to cool roleplaying opportunities, or can be mostly ignored like most other bane are on a regular basis. I really don\u2019t see the problem with it.<br /> <br /> As for the mechanic of the bane itself, I think it\u2019s fine. Lasombras have a drawback with technological devices, have trouble evading cameras, which makes stealth missions harder for them. The lack of reflections has no mechanical impact, but it still can be used to trigger some skill checks to avoid detection in some situations. At least now, we do have a mechanic for it.<br /> To avoid having the bane becoming a derailment to the campaign, while still having some relevance, I think there\u2019s a few scenario where it might apply.<ul><li>A Lasombra got spotted on a camera, while humans are clueless about their true nature, other Kindreds might know. It would be a shame if the Nosferatus got hold of the footage.</li> <li>A Lasombra need to make a phone call to someone as quickly as possible. How do they deal with it?<ul><li>Do they implicate someone else and risk their secret getting spilled out?</li> <li>Do they try to fight their bane and make the phone call on their own, taking the risk of their message not reaching their contact at all?</li> <li>Do they try and use a different means of communication risking their message not reaching their contact in time?</li> </ul></li> <li>The Lasombra want to have a chat with someone from another faction. How do they avoid detection?<ul><li>Do they use email or text messages, leaving traces of their communications?</li> <li>Do they meet with them in person hoping that :<ul><li>A. They don\u2019t get caught doing so.</li> <li>B. The meeting is not gonna turn into a trap.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>There\u2019s a new construction project; a skyscrapper with big reflective windows in the central spot of the Lasombra\u2019s hunting territory. How do they deal with it?</li> </ul>Anyway that\u2019s a few ideas. Everyone is obviously free not to like it but I personally find it to be a gold mine of cool dramatic ideas. Much more so than others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26771,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","user":"Algarik","date":". 09-02-2022, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T09:20:10-07:00","id":1492166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1492084#post1492084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More than the Darkness, which really adds just a little bit of flavour, for me what characterizes Lasombra is that they're agressive, authoritative, and think themselves clever. That Potence + Dominate combination encapsulates what I think of Lasombra. They might be puppet masters, or they might rip and tear. Their chief attributes were strength and manipulation, and their number one ability was intimidation. All three of the Lasombra's disciplines use terror and intimidation.<br /> <br /> A man without a shadow is intimidating. A woman without a reflection is intimidating<br /> A man cursed so that he can't get his phone to work... that's a joke right? Don't get me wrong I like some funny in my WoD but this seems to be vindictive and in poor taste.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pretty much yeah, I've seen a lot of interpretations of the clan as shadowy manulipulators but that only a facet of them. They were made to rule, they can be a Sabbat warlord, a cardinal richoux style figure or a femme fatale or a thousand other things it doesn't matter how you go about it, what matters is you do.<br /> . The truth is at the dark core of the clan is an hunger for power. &quot;Serve none but your ambition, no creed but your will. Desolate as a hurricane, empty of everything but your desire to dominate.&quot; How your pc reacts to this core aspect of the clan is always an interesting angle-do you reject it, moderate it, redirect or embrace it?<br /> <br /> <br /> The origional lasombra clan flaw thematically feeds into this by reflecting (lol) how 'off' and desolate they are. An ironic punishments for their often absurd ego and a warning to others. This is the failure of v5's flaw, it doesn't really mean anything because it mistook motiff (darkness) for theme (shadow), it could be seen as a ironic punishment based on their desire for control but it rapidly degenerates into annoyance and inconvenience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-03-2022, 04:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-03T12:11:02-07:00","id":1492246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1492160#post1492160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it is a very niche aspect, it\u2019s also the one that will have the most impact on how Lasombras will shape their night in the current era.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant about niche wasn't that the Masquerade was niche, it was that <b>the SI threat</b> is niche.<br /> <br /> Your first post specifically called out how their weakness make them that much easier for the SI to get. The SI is a niche aspect that takes a lot of the game when it appears.<br /> <br /> Otherwise you're right, but I didn't argued against that. Actually, no one did. The problem is specifically how the current Bane focus its mechanics on being unable to use tech. The part about reflections and whatnot being a bigger and more interesting aspect is something everyone here agrees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T11:58:25-07:00","id":1492379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1492246#post1492246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I meant about niche wasn't that the Masquerade was niche, it was that <b>the SI threat</b> is niche.<br /> Your first post specifically called out how their weakness make them that much easier for the SI to get. The SI is a niche aspect that takes a lot of the game when it appears.</div> </div> </div> </div>The SI threat is however directly linked to the masquerade, I thought it was heavily implied but maybe I should have been clearer, apologies. My second post was an attempt to explain how the electronic surveillance avoidance penalty the Lasombra suffer, isn\u2019t that niche when the masquerade can imply so much more than the SI only.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1492246#post1492246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise you're right, but I didn't argued against that. Actually, no one did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the impressions that outside of the few interesting answers on how to deal with the \u2018\u2019tech roll\u2019\u2019 we got on the first page of the thread that people were mostly dunking on the new bane for being uninteresting and committing the cardinal sin of being different from previous editions. Which, people here are obviously free to express. I\u2019m not gonna quote the whole thread, as it would be poor form, but I\u2019m gonna quote one of your earlier reply to prove I\u2019m not acting in bad faith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491859#post1491859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably, but it doesn't change things a lot. It is still badly written and, even if it was better written, of dubious interest as a Bane.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one argued against the second part of the bane, but by focusing on the first one and ignoring the second one, of course the bane will be of \u2018\u2019dubious\u2019\u2019 interest, we\u2019re ignoring half of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1492246#post1492246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is specifically how the current Bane focus its mechanics on being unable to use tech.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point. Having just reread, the entry only gives mechanical rules for technology and penalty at avoiding \u2018\u2019electronic vampire systems\u2019\u2019. Which is a bit silly as the book mention them appearing weirdly on cameras.<br /> <br /> Oh well, I guess they could have wrote that part better. In my own games Lasombra will probably suffer from the Nosferatu bane at passing for human, but only for cameras and reflective surfaces. How cool would it be if the older the Lasombra gets, the more twisted their reflection becomes? Up to a point where people can\u2019t simply rationalize it as some kind of glitch or reflective surface irregularities.<br /> <br /> Anyway, not arguing that people should or shouldn\u2019t like the bane. Merely trying to show how it is more than \u2018\u2019dubious\u2019\u2019 of interest. It just needs to be rewritten a bit better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T20:06:36-07:00","id":1492408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1492379#post1492379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got the impressions that outside of the few interesting answers on how to deal with the \u2018\u2019tech roll\u2019\u2019 we got on the first page of the thread that people were mostly dunking on the new bane for being uninteresting and committing the cardinal sin of being different from previous editions. Which, people here are obviously free to express. I\u2019m not gonna quote the whole thread, as it would be poor form, but I\u2019m gonna quote one of your earlier reply to prove I\u2019m not acting in bad faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess this is a common problem with those relatively lengthy threads, usually you have 1 to 3 entire pages of people complaining and making jokes about the bad stuff without yet expressing their ideas better.<br /> <br /> But you quoted my post in page 3, #33. Just a few posts below, #36, I said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491891#post1491891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both are interesting ideas on their own that I think can be worked with, but I actually think the <i>concept</i> of the current one is good, it is the <i>focus</i> on the technology side that's lame.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then started brainstorming ideas for a better mechanic within the exact same concept.<br /> <br /> If you read attentively what everyone posted, no one argued that the weird images are a bad Bane. Some do prefer the old &quot;no reflection at all&quot;, some are less strict about it, but no one derided the concept itself even whe it is not of their liking. The actual rule given and its focus on not being able to use tech properly was the real issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T12:45:55-07:00","id":1492912,"title":"","content":"what kind of darwinistic bane would lead to a stronger clan cohesion though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T23:57:44-07:00","id":1492959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1492912#post1492912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what kind of darwinistic bane would lead to a stronger clan cohesion though.</div> </div> </div> </div>...not appearing in reflections. Seriously. <br /> <br /> It encourages them to be control freaks because anyone noticing such a thing might attract or encourage hunters. It encourages them to be darwinistic because any lasombra that's not good enough could be captured and displayed as an example of -what to look for and so any Lasombra that could likely be captured should instead be destroyed-. Thus being not-culled becomes a source of pride because it shows you're good enough to keep around. Paranoia and Narcisism are encouraged, which in turn encourages more darwinism. <br /> <br /> It's the perfect weakness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T03:27:19-07:00","id":1492967,"title":"","content":"Also, I think it's an interesting counter to the Curse-Of-Ugly that the Nosferatu, Gargoyles and Samedi have. Even when discounting that these clans have magical concealment methods like Obfuscate/Viskeraticka, they do have methods to hide their ugly: I've seen enough of RuPaul's Drag Race to know someone can accomplish miracles with makeup, and honestly speaking most people are polite enough to accept -I have a skin condition/I was in a chemical accident/They Botched the surgery/extreme bodymods are my thing- excuses at face value. However, Lasombra just don't have an excuse. They don't have makeup. They best they can do with clothing is pick something that blends in so people won't expect to see it in a reflection. <i>Maybe </i>they could do something about it with obfuscate. But reflections are too complicated and it'd be difficult to pull that off constantly (plus you're not entirely sure of what you actually look like so getting it accurate could be quite a process) <br /> <br /> <i>Possible headcanon if we ever wanted to replace obtenebration with Obfuscate: The Lasombra are a Nosferatu* lineage that were too vain to ever give up their appearance and instead lost their reflection. They keep Dominate rather than Animalism due to their pride. <br /> *I read somewhere Nosferatu's a second gen, maybe. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T16:26:01-07:00","id":1493079,"title":"","content":"My 2 cents: old Lasombra weakness is too strong, but served 2 purposes: 1) identify them as Vampires &lt;and&gt; Lasombra; 2) make them obsess over their own image (paintings, ghouls that comb and groom them, etc.), because they can't do it perfectly by themselves.<br /> <br /> I like the new &quot;weird in mirrors and cameras&quot;, because it maintains both points whilst &lt;not&gt; being an automatic Masquerade Breach: they still can be identified &lt;IF you know what you are looking for&gt;, and they still &lt;can't see their own image&gt; perfectly (I like to imagine it embossed and/or distorted, so they can be recognized, but you can't see fine details - you couldn't draw him based on his reflection alone).<br /> <br /> About the Tech roll, I understand it to be &quot;tech savvy&quot; to use different strategies, such as &quot;did you know some smartphones accept input if you press this and that physical button, but only for such and such actions?&quot;. But I really think it shouldn't exist, I'd made it simply something on the lines of penalty in Technology rolls &lt;as a factor of&gt; Bane Level coupled with Tech acts &quot;glitchy&quot; near them if they fail their roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T17:56:22-07:00","id":1493087,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the bottom line is that the rules on the Bane should have focused on the actually interesting main concept instead of making it in practice about the tech roll. A nice example of good idea/bad execution. Nothing extremely hard to fix, either, just kinda embarrassing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T17:07:25-07:00","id":1509799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway#post1491391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like if they try to use a cell-phone, does the roll represent them taking it apart and putting it back together? Something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my chronicles Lasombra need a crit to use phone. I made it difficult, and lore-wise I explain it as Oblivion not being in the same state at all times. In my chronicle is fluent, making the Technology very difficult, but not impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27765-euderos","name":"Euderos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27765_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T00:55:14-07:00","id":1509846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1493087#post1493087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the bottom line is that the rules on the Bane should have focused on the actually interesting main concept instead of making it in practice about the tech roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>The V5 Lasombra Weakness / Bane seems too like too troublesome or problematic quality to me. I think that it should during some situations produce minor disruptions or occurences in regard some technology, including rolling to see if this happens. Lasombra Vampires should have no problems or limitations in regard to standard (and more specific / particular ) interaction, use, and repairing of machinery, devices, electronics, computers, and other technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T04:04:06-07:00","id":1510873,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the thread necromancy but I've just had an idea for lasombra clan flaw<br /> <br /> Keep the old flaw then ad a rule that a fail on a social roll is an immediate reveal if mirrors are present and if for less prominent reflective surfaces a botch lasombra still show up completly fine on digital media so no stealth perk.<br /> <br /> nice and simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T05:49:36-07:00","id":1510875,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I always preferred the Xi Dundu weakness<br /> The weakness of the Xi Dundu is similar to the Lasombra weakness of casting no reflection; the Xi Dundu <i>cast no shadow</i> of any sort.<br /> Also, the they must not be touched by their native soil when they rest else they are greatly weakened; this is perhaps a further reflection of their original banishing sincwe as the legend go, the Xi Dundu originally hailed from the Congo until a rite gone wrong forced them from their homelands...<br /> Anyhow, the Lasombra would totally could have the cast no shadow of any short weakness; maybe they lost their own to the Abyss (or it gain sentinence and wandered off, a bit like Peter Pan's) or during the Embrace-ritual, since the Lasombra are usually ambitious, sneaky, ruthless, shrewd, and manipulative, could totally see, they cast their own shadow out, so no one could see them coming from behind (and probably that Shadow is offended and seek revenge...)<br /> Even the must not be touched by their native soil when they rest could be a nice one, explained by the Lasombra seafaring nature or their connection to the primal darkness that existed before God decreed &quot;<i>Let there be Light&quot; </i>so their own homland rejects them; would be a curious contrast to the Tzimisce weakness.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T12:02:51-07:00","id":1510902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1510873#post1510873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the thread necromancy but I've just had an idea for lasombra clan flaw<br /> <br /> Keep the old flaw then ad a rule that a fail on a social roll is an immediate reveal if mirrors are present and if for less prominent reflective surfaces a botch lasombra still show up completly fine on digital media so no stealth perk.<br /> <br /> nice and simple.</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me of something I've thought for a long time: why shouldn't vampires get a stealth perk from not showing up on mirrors and cameras? They gave werewolves free mass forgetful mind just to make their lives easier. I'm very tempted to just have all vampires not show up in mirrors and cameras except when they blush of life. It would just be this neat little thing that sometimes makes keeping the masquerade easier, and other times makes it harder, situationally.<br /> <br /> Vampires have enough problems staying hidden without every camera catching them do every little thing.<br /> <br /> The only problem I see with the no reflection/camera thing is making it clan-specific. It should just be this general vampire thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T04:38:38-07:00","id":1512709,"title":"","content":"Well, I think bizarre that the main Ventrue's competitors were so nerfed. They lost their signature power, they have a hard time using technology, and they lost their sect. I don't know what the poor Lasombras did to deserve that, but they have gone down hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T05:06:22-07:00","id":1512712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1491416#post1491416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why they need a &quot;flaw&quot; in V5. They degenerate using their signature discipline, which also sucks, and their other disciplines are the hardest hit by the new edition. Add to that their political situation and they're easily the most shafted clan in the game even before tech problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every clan needs a curse and we agree that not having a reflection could be a problem for the mask, but it would hardly be something narratively problematic, it would just justify them acting in the shadows a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T06:07:44-07:00","id":1512715,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> I beg to differ<br /> Vampire is a personal horror game, and not having reflection is one of the most - if not <i>the</i> most - devastating flaws I could immagine<br /> <br /> Aside the usual the inability to see their <i>reflection</i>, many became slightly obsessed with their appearance-thing the inability to see yourself could be (should be!) traumatic<br /> Your face, your appearance that you inherited from your ancestors is You. Part what and who you are. Even if you became horrily disfigured, like a Samedi or Nosferatu, somewhere in your horrifying visage, you can find <i>yourself </i><br /> But if you can't see yourself?<br /> Thats terrible.<br /> How long it would take to <i>forget </i>your own face?<br /> You are the mightiest of the predators, you could be noble, ritch, mighty blood god... yet the humblest little prey could see himself in a pond, a mirror, or anything... <i>you can not</i>. You are unable to do so.<br /> (arguably, the Flaw <b>Death\u2019s Reflection </b>is even worse, You cast a reflection normally, which would cancel out the clan weakness \u2013 except that your reflection always shows the state that you\u2019d be in if you were dead. Any Lasombra more than a few decades old looks in reflection like an ambling skeleton. Younger vampires appear as rotting corpses. This is insane, Dorian Gray eat your heart out)<br /> And you can up the stake so to speak!<br /> Are you even real?<br /> Many myths the vampire's body is... just an illusion, a mirage, something not real, and thats why they cast no reflection<br /> <br /> There is a great deal of folklore associated with mirrors, including the belief that the soul projects out of the body and into mirrors in the form of reflection. This belief underlies the most widely known mirror superstition; that breaking a mirror brings seven years of bad luck. Many cultures believe that breaking a mirror also breaks the soul of the one who broke it. The soul, angered at being hurt, exacts seven years of bad luck in payment for such carelessness. The Romans attributed the bad luck to their belief that life renews itself every seven years. To break mirror meant breaking one's health, and this could not be remedied for seven years. In some cultures, breaking a mirror was thought to presage a death in the family. This association of mirrors with death is common and stems from the belief that the soul can become trapped in the mirror. For this reason, children were often not allowed to look in a mirror until they were at least one year old. Mirrors were covered during sleep and illness so that the soul, in its wanderings, would not become trapped and unable to return to the body. After a death, mirrors were also covered to prevent the soul of the newly departed from becoming caught in the mirror, delaying its journey to the afterlife.<br /> When Native Americans were faced with Ni\u00e9pce and Daguerre\u2019s invention, they believed the camera was capturing their soul, not just their appearance, stealing it from them and therefore they feared these intricate devices.<br /> <br /> \u201cA mirror can contain the reflection of the whole universe, a whole skyful of stars in a piece of silvered glass no thicker than a breath.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhen you stand between two mirrors you\u2019re spread out among the images, your whole soul is pulled out thin, and somewhere in the distant images a dark part of you might get out and come looking for you, if you aren\u2019t careful.<br /> <br /> Two amazing quote from Sir Terry Pratchett<br /> <br /> Back to the topic, not having a reflection, could mean you lost your soul... forever.<br /> Every night you reminded you don't have it, and without a soul who you are?<br /> <br /> In my peronsal opinion, not having a reflection could destroy a vampire's sanity in a short few... jesus, months even, not just years and I always put heavy emphasis on this flaw if one of my players are foolish enough to be a Lasombra, because their flaw is an existential nightmare and the qintessence of personal horror<br /> A few Clan Flaw is like that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T06:35:35-07:00","id":1512719,"title":"","content":"It's a good point, and it really makes a whole new sense of a Garou needing a reflected surface to access the Umbra. This would also explain why some Lasombra are so inhuman, after all, to live with or just not care about the lack of reflection would be demanding too much from most people, in which case the curse seems to work like a sieve. However, being practical, each clan's weakness needs to have some impact on how you play mechanically as well and merely a lack of reflex would only limit the places you can interact with, which is ultimately left for the narrator to resolve, otherwise you have to a clan that in practice has no weakness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T07:44:41-07:00","id":1512730,"title":"","content":"I disagree: not seeing your own face is unnerving but something I think most people can deal with. Perhaps if you were a little too narcissistic it would bother you (well, maybe a narcissist would be self assured enough) <br /> <br /> For me, it's the paranoia/ control freak aspect. <br /> You can't go near busy car streets because cars all have mirrors on them and a driver might just notice and cause a scene or draw trouble. Massive threat. <br /> big Windows in shopping districts or some modern business districts are a minor threat, some have mirrors by the window, your enemies might just encourage more mirrors in these places to fuck with you. <br /> Many clubs are fond of big mirrors. So your selection is limited. <i>Hey maybe all the clubs having mirrors is a ventrue conspiracy</i>. <br /> Night, rain, hard surfaces, lights: if you've ever lived in a town or city where these things come together, you know they'll drive up paranoia. It's probably why Lasombra like places bordering the Mediterranean but don't seem to care for the Baltic: the water stays around for longer in the north. <br /> Your own childer need to be very carefully selected because well, if they're captured, it'll<i> reflect</i> back on you. Imagine it: a hunter finds your reflectionless child, suddenly they start moving round the city, or lurking in the windows of high traffic areas, looking for anyone without a reflection, This is why Lasombra are so extreme with their 'unworthy lasombra should die' attitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T07:52:41-07:00","id":1512733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1512730#post1512730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree: not seeing your own face is unnerving but something I think most people can deal with. Perhaps if you were a little too narcissistic it would bother you (well, maybe a narcissist would be self assured enough)<br /> <br /> For me, it's the paranoia/ control freak aspect.<br /> You can't go near busy car streets because cars all have mirrors on them and a driver might just notice and cause a scene or draw trouble. Massive threat.<br /> big Windows in shopping districts or some modern business districts are a minor threat, some have mirrors by the window, your enemies might just encourage more mirrors in these places to fuck with you.<br /> Many clubs are fond of big mirrors. So your selection is limited. <i>Hey maybe all the clubs having mirrors is a ventrue conspiracy</i>.<br /> Night, rain, hard surfaces, lights: if you've ever lived in a town or city where these things come together, you know they'll drive up paranoia. It's probably why Lasombra like places bordering the Mediterranean but don't seem to care for the Baltic: the water stays around for longer in the north.<br /> Your own childer need to be very carefully selected because well, if they're captured, it'll<i> reflect</i> back on you. Imagine it: a hunter finds your reflectionless child, suddenly they start moving round the city, or lurking in the windows of high traffic areas, looking for anyone without a reflection, This is why Lasombra are so extreme with their 'unworthy lasombra should die' attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the Sabbat don't they usually embrace several to use as shock troops?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T08:47:23-07:00","id":1512741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1512733#post1512733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the Sabbat don't they usually embrace several to use as shock troops?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they survive, they might be worthy! In any case, the scrutiny never ends. A 300 year old vampire can be deemed unworthy just as a fledgling can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T15:33:57-07:00","id":1512780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491391-what-does-the-lasombra-s-technology-roll-represent-them-doing-anyway?p=1512733#post1512733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the Sabbat don't they usually embrace several to use as shock troops?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is good to remember that these Cainites are definitely to at least a meaningful and considerable extent sisters and brothers from the Sabbat, who in the future can become contributing, trustworthy, and normal Sabb